    {
      "id": "cef1f2882f2c-q1",
      "number": 1,
      "question": "AB is a chord of a circle of radius 10 meters. If AB = 10 meters, then the length of the arc AB of the circle is approximately",
      "questionHtml": "AB is a chord of a circle of radius 10 meters. If AB = 10 meters, then the length of the arc AB of the circle is approximately",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "10.4 meter",
          "html": "10.4 meter"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "10.5 meter",
          "html": "10.5 meter"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "10.2 meter",
          "html": "10.2 meter"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "10.3 meter",
          "html": "10.3 meter"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given: </strong></p>\n\n<p>Chord = Radius = 10 meters</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>OA = OB = AB = 10 m</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/01/F1_Vinanti_State%20govt._03.01.23_D1.png\" style=\"height: 193px; width: 193px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>&Delta;OAB is an equilateral triangle so all angles will be 60&deg;</p>\n\n<p>Now</p>\n\n<p>&ang;AOB = 60&deg;</p>\n\n<p>So, the arc of the circle = (&theta;/360&deg;) &times; (2&pi;r)</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; (60/360) &times; (2 &times; 22/7 &times; 10)</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 10.47 &asymp; 10.5 m</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The required result will be 10.5.</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/01/F1_Vinanti_State%20govt._03.01.23_D1.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cef1f2882f2c-q2",
      "number": 2,
      "question": "In a circle with center O, a diameter PQ is produced to a point R lying outside the circle and RS is a tangent to the circle at the point T on it. If &ang;PRT = 50&deg;, then what is the measure of &ang;QTR?",
      "questionHtml": "In a circle with center O, a diameter PQ is produced to a point R lying outside the circle and RS is a tangent to the circle at the point T on it. If &ang;PRT = 50&deg;, then what is the measure of &ang;QTR?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "20 &deg;",
          "html": "20<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "43 &deg;",
          "html": "43<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "75 &deg;",
          "html": "75<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "85 &deg;",
          "html": "85<span style=\"\">&deg;</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Given:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&ang;PRT = 50&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Concept used:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">The tangent at any point of a circle is perpendicular to the radius through the point of contact.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">The sum of the interior angles of a triangle is 180<span style=\"\">&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Calculation:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/04/F1_Shraddha_SSC_06.04.2022_D3.png\" style=\"width: 337px; height: 210px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&Delta;OTR is a right-angled triangle at T.</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Hence,&nbsp;<span style=\"\">&ang;ROT = (180 - 90 - 50)&deg; = 40&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&Delta;OQT is an isosceles triangle since OQ = OT (Radii of the circle)</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&ang;OTQ =&nbsp;&ang;OQT = (180 - 40)&nbsp;&divide; 2 = 70&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&ang;OTR =&nbsp;&ang;OTQ +&nbsp;&ang;QTR</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr; 90&deg; = 70&deg; +&nbsp;&ang;QTR</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr;</span>&nbsp;&ang;QTR = 20<span style=\"\">&deg;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong><span style=\"\">&there4; The measure of the&nbsp;&ang;QTR is 20&deg;.</span></strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/04/F1_Shraddha_SSC_06.04.2022_D3.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cef1f2882f2c-q3",
      "number": 3,
      "question": "In the following figure, &Delta;ABC is an inscribed triangle as shown and DE is a tangent to the circle at C. If m&ang;ACD = 65&deg; and m&ang;ACB = 35&deg;, find the measure of m&ang;BAC.",
      "questionHtml": "<p>In the following figure,&nbsp;&Delta;ABC is an inscribed triangle as shown and DE is a tangent to the circle at C. If m&ang;ACD = 65&deg; and m&ang;ACB = 35&deg;, find the measure of m&ang;BAC.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/11/F2_Savita_SSC_16-11-22_D6.png\" style=\"width: 158px; height: 198px;\" /></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "80&deg;",
          "html": "80&deg;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "75&deg;",
          "html": "75&deg;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "60&deg;",
          "html": "60&deg;&nbsp;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "65&deg;",
          "html": "65&deg;&nbsp;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "A",
      "solution": "<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">∠BAC = ∠BCE</p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">Here, in ΔABC, ∠BCE + ∠ACB + ∠ACD = 180° ⇒∠BCE + 35° + 65° = 180° ⇒∠BCE + 100° = 180° ⇒∠BAC = 80°          ---- From equation (1) </p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/11/F2_Savita_SSC_16-11-22_D6.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cef1f2882f2c-q4",
      "number": 4,
      "question": "In a circle, two chords BA and DC intersect outside the circle at point P and at the same time chord DA and BC intersects inside the circle at point Q. If BQ = 5 cm, AQ = 15 cm, DQ = 3 cm, PA = 5 cm, PB = 6 cm and PD = 15 cm then find the ratio of PC and CQ.",
      "questionHtml": "In a circle, two chords BA and DC intersect outside the circle at point P and at the same time chord DA and BC intersects inside the circle at point Q. If BQ = 5 cm, AQ = 15 cm, DQ = 3 cm, PA = 5 cm, PB = 6 cm and PD = 15 cm then find the ratio of PC and CQ.",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "2 : 7",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">2 : 7</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "7 : 9",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">7 : 9</span>"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "2 : 9",
          "html": "2 : 9"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "9 : 2",
          "html": "<span style=\"\">9 : 2</span>"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">In a circle, </span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Chords AB and CD intersect outside the circle at point P.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">Chord DA and BC intersect inside the circle at point Q.</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">BQ = 5 cm, AQ = 15 cm, DQ = 3 cm, PA = 5 cm, PB = 6 cm and PD = 15 cm</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\"><strong>Formula&nbsp;used:</strong></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">When two chords intersect&nbsp;inside the circle.</span></p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F2_Madhuri_Railways_31.05.2022_D15.png\" style=\"height: 175px; width: 175px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>AO&nbsp;&times; OC = OB&nbsp;&times; OD</p>\n\n<p>When two chords intersect outside the circle.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F2_Madhuri_Railways_31.05.2022_D21.png\" style=\"height: 128px; width: 208px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>BE&nbsp;&times; AE = EC&nbsp;&times; ED</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>According to the question, the required image is:</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F2_Madhuri_Railways_31.05.2022_D17.png\" style=\"height: 128px; width: 211px;\" /></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">For&nbsp;two chords intersect outside the circle:</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">PA&nbsp;&times; PB = PC&nbsp;&times; PD</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">&rArr; 5&nbsp;&times; 6 = PC&nbsp;&times; 15</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; PC = 2 cm</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">For&nbsp;two chords intersect inside&nbsp;the circle:</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">BQ &times; QC&nbsp;= AQ&nbsp;&times; QD</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; 5&nbsp;&times; CQ&nbsp;= 15 &times; 3</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; CQ&nbsp;= 9&nbsp;cm</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Now,&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">&rArr; PC : CQ = 2 : 9</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>&there4; The required ratio is 2 : 9.</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F2_Madhuri_Railways_31.05.2022_D15.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F2_Madhuri_Railways_31.05.2022_D21.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/05/F2_Madhuri_Railways_31.05.2022_D17.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cef1f2882f2c-q5",
      "number": 5,
      "question": "In a circular field, AOB and COD are two mutually perpendicular diameters having length of 4 meters. X is the mid-point of OA. Y is a point on the circumference such that &ang;YOD = 30&deg;. Which of the following correctly gives the relation among the three alternate paths from X to Y?",
      "questionHtml": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/07/F1_Vinanti_Defence_17.07.23_D8.png\" style=\"width: 139px; height: 140px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>In a circular field, AOB and COD are two mutually perpendicular diameters having length of 4 meters. X is the mid-point of OA. Y is a point on the circumference such that &ang;YOD = 30&deg;. Which of the following correctly gives the relation among the three alternate paths from X to Y?</p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "XOBY ∶ XODY ∶ XADY ∶∶ 5.15 ∶ 4.50 ∶ 5.06",
          "html": "XOBY ∶ XODY ∶ XADY ∶∶ 5.15 ∶ 4.50 ∶ 5.06"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "XADY ∶ XODY ∶ XOBY ∶∶ 6.25 ∶ 5.34 ∶ 4.24",
          "html": "XADY ∶ XODY ∶ XOBY ∶∶ 6.25 ∶ 5.34 ∶ 4.24"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "XODY ∶ XOBY ∶ XADY ∶∶ 4.04 ∶ 5.35 ∶ 5.25",
          "html": "XODY ∶ XOBY ∶ XADY ∶∶ 4.04 ∶ 5.35 ∶ 5.25"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "XADY ∶ XOBY ∶ XODY ∶∶ 5.19 ∶ 5.09 ∶ 4.04",
          "html": "XADY ∶ XOBY ∶ XODY ∶∶ 5.19 ∶ 5.09 ∶ 4.04"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p>AOB &perp;&nbsp;COD &amp; X is the mid-point of OA.</p>\n\n<p>AOB = COD = 4 m</p>\n\n<p>AX = OX</p>\n\n<p>Y is a point on the circumference such that &ang;YOD = 30&deg;.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Formula used:</strong></p>\n\n<p>The perimeter of the circle of radius = 2&pi;r</p>\n\n<p>Length of an arc having angle&nbsp;&theta; in the center = 2&pi;r&nbsp;&times; (&theta;/360&deg;)</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong><br />\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/07/F1_Vinanti_Defence_17.07.23_D8.png\" style=\"width: 139px; height: 140px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>From the figure,</p>\n\n<p>AO = (1/2)AOB = 2 m&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>AX = (1/2) AO = 1 m</p>\n\n<p>Now,</p>\n\n<p>Perimeter of circle = 2&pi;r = 4&pi;</p>\n\n<p>XADY = XA + ADY&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">XADY&nbsp;</span>= 1 + 4&pi; &times;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{120}{360} = 1 + \\frac{4 π}{3}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">XADY&nbsp;</span> = 5.19</strong></p>\n\n<p>Similarly,&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">XOBY&nbsp;</span>= XO + OB + 4&pi;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{60}{360}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">XOBY = 1 + 2 + 4&pi;&nbsp;&times; (1/6)&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><strong>XOBY =</strong>&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">5.09&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p>Again,</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-family: var(--bs-body-font-family); font-size: var(--bs-body-font-size); font-weight: var(--bs-body-font-weight); text-align: var(--bs-body-text-align);\">XODY = XO + OD + DY</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">XODY&nbsp;= 1 + 2 + 4&pi; &times;&nbsp;<span class=\"math-tex\">\\(\\frac{30}{360}\\)</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\"><span style=\"font-weight: bolder;\">XODY&nbsp;= 4.04</span></p>\n\n<p><strong>XADY ∶ XOBY ∶ XODY <span style=\"color: rgb(33, 37, 41);\">∶∶</span> 5.19 ∶ 5.09 ∶ 4.04</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/23/07/F1_Vinanti_Defence_17.07.23_D8.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cef1f2882f2c-q6",
      "number": 6,
      "question": "In the given figure, AB is the diameter of a circle with center O and AT is a tangent if &ang;AOQ = 68&deg;, then what is &ang;ATQ?",
      "questionHtml": "<p>In the given figure, AB is the diameter of a circle with center O and AT is a tangent if &ang;AOQ = 68&deg;, then what is &ang;ATQ?&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/25/08/Screenshot%202025-08-07%20160643.png\" style=\"width: 305px; height: 219px;\" /></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "65&deg;",
          "html": "65&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "62&deg;",
          "html": "62&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "56&deg;",
          "html": "56&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "51&deg;",
          "html": "51&deg;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p>AB is the diameter of the circle</p>\n\n<p>AT is tangent to the circle at point A</p>\n\n<p>&ang;AOQ = 68&deg;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Formula used:</strong></p>\n\n<p>1. Angle made by same chord at center is twice the angle made at the circle</p>\n\n<p>2. Use angle sum property in triangle ABT: &ang;ABT + &ang;BAT + &ang;ATB = 180&deg;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculations:</strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"color:  (33, 37, 41);\">&ang;AOQ = 68&deg; &rArr; &ang;ABQ = 34&deg; (using chord AQ)</span></p>\n\n<p>&ang;ABT = 34&deg;</p>\n\n<p>AT is tangent, &ang;BAT = 90&deg;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; &ang;ATQ = 180&deg; - (90&deg; + 34&deg;) = 56&deg;</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; &ang;ATQ = 56&deg;</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/25/08/Screenshot%202025-08-07%20160643.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cef1f2882f2c-q7",
      "number": 7,
      "question": "In a circle, AB and DC are two chords. When AB and DC are produced, they meet at P. If PC = 2.8 cm, PB = 3.15 cm and AB = 3.85 cm, then CD = ?",
      "questionHtml": "<p>In a circle, AB and DC are two chords. When AB and DC are produced, they meet at P. If PC = 2.8 cm, PB = 3.15 cm and AB = 3.85 cm, then CD = ?</p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "6.975 cm",
          "html": "6.975 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "5.075 cm",
          "html": "5.075 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "4.175 cm",
          "html": "4.175 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "7.875 cm",
          "html": "7.875 cm"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "B",
      "solution": "<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Given:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">AB and DC are two chords. They are produced to meet at P.</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">PC = 2.8 cm, PB = 3.15 cm and AB = 3.85 cm,</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Concept used:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/04/F2_Savita_SSC_08-4-22_D1.png\" style=\"height: 108px; width: 239px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Here, PA &amp; PC are two secants and PT is a tangent at point T on the circle.&nbsp;<br />\nSo, we know,<br />\nPA&nbsp;&times; PB =&nbsp; PC&nbsp;&times; PD = (PT)<span style=\" line-height: 0; position: relative; vertical-align: baseline; top: -0.5em;font-size:10.5px;\">2</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"font-weight: 700;\">Calculation:</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/04/F2_Savita_SSC_08-4-22_D2.png\" style=\"width: 221px; height: 103px;\" /></p>\n\n<p style=\"\">So, PA = AB + PB = 3.15 + 3.85 = 7 cm</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">Now,</p>\n\n<p style=\"\">PA&nbsp;&times; PB = PD&nbsp;&times; PC</p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr; 7&nbsp;&times; 3.15 = PD&nbsp;&times; 2.8&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr; PD = 7.875</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr; PC + CD = 7.875</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><span style=\"\">&rArr; CD = 5.075</span></p>\n\n<p style=\"\"><strong>&there4; The length of CD&nbsp; is 5.075 cm.</strong></p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/04/F2_Savita_SSC_08-4-22_D1.png",
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/04/F2_Savita_SSC_08-4-22_D2.png"
      ],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cef1f2882f2c-q8",
      "number": 8,
      "question": "There are two circles C1, and C2 of radii 5 cm and 7 cm respectively. The common transverse tangent touches the circles at points P and Q respectively. The line joining the centres of the circles intersects the tangent at X. The distance of X from the centre of the smaller circle is 13 cm. What is the length of the line segment PQ?",
      "questionHtml": "There are two circles C1, and C2 of radii 5 cm and 7 cm respectively. The common transverse tangent touches the circles at points P and Q respectively. The line joining the centres of the circles intersects the tangent at X. The distance of X from the centre of the smaller circle is 13 cm. What is the length of the line segment PQ?",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "23.2 cm",
          "html": "23.2 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "18 cm",
          "html": "18 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "28.8 cm",
          "html": "28.8 cm"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "30 cm",
          "html": "30 cm"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p>The radii of the two circles are 5&nbsp;cm and 7&nbsp;cm</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"\">The distance of X from the centre of the smaller circle is 13 cm.</span></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"\">Concept used:</span></strong></p>\n\n<p>Two triangles are similar if all angles are equal and the ratio of the corresponding sides of the similar triangles are equal.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/09/F2_Savita_SSC_12-9-22_D5.png\" /></p>\n\n<p>Let A and B be the centres of the circle</p>\n\n<p>AP = 5 cm (radius of the smaller circle), BQ = 7cm (radius of the bigger circle)</p>\n\n<p>AX = 13 cm&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>So in&nbsp;&Delta;APX, using Pythagoras theorem,</p>\n\n<p>PX<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;+ AP<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;= AX<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;&rArr;&nbsp;PX<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;= 13<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;- 5<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; PX = 12 cm</p>\n\n<p>&Delta;APX and&nbsp;&Delta;BQX are similar to each other as all angles are equal.</p>\n\n<p>&there4; AP/BQ = PX/QX (∵ ratio of the corresponding sides of the similar triangle are equal)</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 5/7 = 12/QX</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; QX = 12&nbsp;&times; 7/5 = 84/5 = 16.8 cm</p>\n\n<p>Now, PQ = PX + QX = 12 + 16.8 = 28.8 cm</p>\n\n<p>&there4; The length of the line segment PQ is 28.8 cm</p>\n",
      "images": [
        "https://storage.googleapis.com/tb-img/production/22/09/F2_Savita_SSC_12-9-22_D5.png"
      ],
