    {
      "id": "cef1f2882f2c-q10",
      "number": 10,
      "question": "In the given figure, O is the centre of the circle. If the angles &ang;AOB, &ang;OAC are, respectively, 140&deg; and 50&deg;, then the value of angle &ang;BAC is ______.",
      "questionHtml": "<p><!-- x-tinymce/html -->In the given figure, O is the centre of the circle. If the angles &ang;AOB, &ang;OAC are, respectively, 140&deg; and 50&deg;, then the value of angle &ang;BAC is ______.</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/images/production/quesImages/qImage67c2ad44c7dc6376376cbe2f.png\" /></p>\n",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "60&deg;",
          "html": "60&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "50&deg;",
          "html": "50&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "30&deg;",
          "html": "30&deg;"
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "80&deg;",
          "html": "80&deg;"
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "C",
      "solution": "<p><strong>Given:</strong></p>\n\n<p>O is the center of the circle.</p>\n\n<p>&ang;AOB = 140&deg;</p>\n\n<p>&ang;OAC = 50&deg;</p>\n\n<p><strong>Formula Used:</strong></p>\n\n<p>Angle subtended by an arc at the center is double the angle subtended by the same arc at any point on the remaining part of the circle.</p>\n\n<p>In a triangle, angles opposite to equal sides are equal.</p>\n\n<p>Sum of angles in a triangle is 180&deg;.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Calculation:</strong></p>\n\n<p>Consider triangle OAC. Since OA and OC are radii of the same circle, OA = OC.</p>\n\n<p>Therefore, &ang;OCA = &ang;OAC = 50&deg; (angles opposite to equal sides are equal).</p>\n\n<p>In triangle OAC, &ang;AOC + &ang;OAC + &ang;OCA = 180&deg; (sum of angles in a triangle).</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; &ang;AOC + 50&deg; + 50&deg; = 180&deg;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; &ang;AOC + 100&deg; = 180&deg;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; &ang;AOC = 180&deg; - 100&deg;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; &ang;AOC = 80&deg;</p>\n\n<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"//cdn.testbook.com/images/production/quesImages/qImage6829b0fe2f7d0099bb2eb656.png\" style=\"height: 242px; width: 250px;\" /></p>\n\n<p>The reflex angle &ang;AOC at the center is 360&deg; - &ang;AOC = 360&deg; - 80&deg; = 280&deg;.</p>\n\n<p>Angle subtended by arc ABC at the center is reflex &ang;AOC = 280&deg;.</p>\n\n<p>Angle subtended by arc ABC at the circumference is &ang;ABC.</p>\n\n<p>&ang;ABC = (1/2) &times; reflex &ang;AOC = (1/2) &times; 280&deg; = 140&deg;.</p>\n\n<p>Consider triangle OAB. Since OA and OB are radii of the same circle, OA = OB.</p>\n\n<p>Therefore, &ang;OBA = &ang;OAB.</p>\n\n<p>In triangle OAB, &ang;AOB + &ang;OAB + &ang;OBA = 180&deg;.</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 140&deg; + &ang;OAB + &ang;OAB = 180&deg;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 140&deg; + 2&ang;OAB = 180&deg;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 2&ang;OAB = 180&deg; - 140&deg;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; 2&ang;OAB = 40&deg;</p>\n\n<p>&rArr; &ang;OAB = 20&deg;</p>\n\n<p>&ang;BAC = &ang;OAC - &ang;OAB = 50&deg; - 20&deg; = 30&deg;.</p>\n\n<p><strong>&there4; The value of angle &ang;BAC is 30&deg;.</strong></p>\n",
